  "body": "Selecting English still left the public directory's search, filters, errors, metadata and accessible names in Spanish. Sharing also discarded rejected promises, so cancelling the native dialog caused an uncaught page error. Use the existing ES/EN catalogs throughout discovery and map controls, retain public identities and input across language changes, and give accurate sharing/clipboard cancellation and recovery feedback.\n\nDepends on #447; its latest c7124f906 recovery fix is merged into this branch with unchanged verified product files. Merge #447 first. The focused addition is commit f59aa583b; the dependency merge preserves its source hashes.\n\nValidation: 26 component/helper tests and ten ES/EN production-bundle journeys pass across three engines/five profiles. Includes delayed/failed search, retry, ambiguous favorite write with authoritative refresh, error dismissal, sharing cancellation, denied clipboard followed by explicit successful copy, geolocation denial, map labels and axe. TypeScript/lint/build pass (367923 gzip initial JS); strict catalog audit passes for all 1138 candidates. Browser APIs/platform dialogs are controlled fixtures, not proof of real provider delivery or backend persistence. Required CI remains pending.\n\nUpdates the existing UX006/UX047 findings, coverage, versioned screenshots and release checkpoint. Production API remains5c11577; new changes are not deployed. Apple remains WAITING_FOR_REVIEW with AFTER_APPROVAL; final mobile publication and physical-device gates remain unfinished. No migration or new provider is introduced.\n",
